<title>UK: Allgemeine Hypo plans to add 500 mln marks to bond.</title>
<headline>Allgemeine Hypo plans to add 500 mln marks to bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allgemeine Hypothekenbank plans to add 500 million marks to its 5.25 percent Pfandbrief, joint lead managers Commerzbank, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Dresdner Kleinwort Benson and HSBC Trinkaus said on Monday.</p>
<p>The 1.5 billion mark bond matures in February 2005.</p>
<p>The increase planned for Tuesday will be dependent on market conditions they added, with a launch spread of 11-12 basis points over the 7.375 percent 2005 Bund.  </p>
<p>AHB's Pfandbriefe are rated Aa2 by Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
